  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">222437_Start Network Anticipation of Dzud 2024 Mongolia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">* Project site: Gobi-Altai , Uvs, Zavkhan, Sukhbaatar and Dornod
 
 * Partner Agency: Save the Children Japan
 
 * This project provides the following three forms of assistance to around 1,200 most affected households and 5,866 children.
 
 1) Multi-purpose cash transfer: Cash up to GBP 152 will be distributed to each herder household to support critical input for food security, health, emergency communications, and other basic needs, especially for children. Cash also allows for the families to have the flexibility to prioritise and fulfil their own needs. 
 
 2) Livestock fodder: Each family will receive 160-200 kg of livestock fodder. Provision of fodder will keep away herders from spending distributed cash to buy fodder, and enable families to meet other basic needs such as food, hygiene and sanitation. 
 
 3) Psychological First Aid Training (PFA): PFA training of the trainers will be provided for 76 dormitory teachers and specialists of emergency management, education, child welfare and social policy departments. These trainers will reach 5,866 herder children who stay at the rural dormitories. The Partner Agency(StC) will conduct the PFA training for dormitory teachers of all soums(provinces) of target aims, staff of emergency management, education and child development departments. The participants will be equipped with the tools to detect early signs of distress, raise awareness among children on coping skills, and refer to specialists if required.</narrative>
  </description>
